Milamber-Wiz-Hum-Mal-Cha died on the Astral Plane.
Killed by Pestilence (with the Amulet).

Pesty got his hands on an amulet of reflection, and that was my undoing.

I'd headed to the right on Astral, but it was the lawful altar.  Trying to
fight my way back, I was getting beat up by the priests and angels.  Then
along comes Pesty with his shiny new amulet, sickening me over and over.
Ran out of mana and eventually couldn't cure my sickness (despite dropping
the Amulet).  Prayed but didn't get my HP restored.  Quaffed four potions of
full healing and got through three amulets of life saving.

Is it me, or does carrying the Amulet have an unbalanced effect on
spellcasters as opposed to fighters?  The mana drain was terrible - and a
spellcaster's primary means of both offence and defence are his spells.  The
Knight and Valk I ascended recently never felt as though they were being
penalised anything like that much for carrying the Amulet.

Strangely enough, the other Planes felt easier this time then previously.  I
maintain that if Pestilence hadn't had that amulet of reflection, I would
have made it.  Guess it shows what a difference one piece of kit can make.
Oh, for a cockatrice corpse...

